[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 703,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 466,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106700,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 214,
        "headingId": 466,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Chondromesenchymal hamartoma of the chest wall is a benign tumour composed of cartilage, spindle cells, bone, and blood-filled cystic spaces.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T15:24:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 704,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 467,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106701,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 214,
        "headingId": 467,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T15:24:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 705,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 468,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106702,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 214,
        "headingId": 468,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F01 Benign neoplasm of intrathoracic organs</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T15:24:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 706,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 469,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106703,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 214,
        "headingId": 469,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> chest wall hamartoma; cartilaginous hamartoma; cartilaginous hamartoma of the chest wall; (benign) mesenchymoma; vascular and giant chondromatous hamartoma of the chest wall.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T15:24:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 707,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 470,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106704,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 214,
        "headingId": 470,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T15:24:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 708,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 471,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106705,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 214,
        "headingId": 471,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lesions arise within the medullary cavity or on the surface (mostly lateral and posterior regions) of a rib and may extend into multiple contiguous ribs. Bilateral or multicentric tumours have been reported {3969297; 8861490; 11756727; 16703172; 18181344}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T15:24:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 709,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 472,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106706,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 214,
        "headingId": 472,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Infants may be asymptomatic or present with respiratory distress as a result of rib deformation and involvement of the chest cavity {3763502; 8166533; 8291008; 1409151; 18181344}. The mass may be palpable, or it may be detected incidentally on a chest radiograph for an upper respiratory tract infection {8166533; 8861490; 11756727; 18416338}.</p>\r\n<h5>Imaging</h5>\r\n<p>Plain radiography shows a well-defined lytic lesion with a sclerotic margin and an extrapleural soft tissue mass. The lesion has a solid and cystic appearance, more evident on CT. Haemorrhagic cavities with a secondary aneurysmal bone cyst&ndash;like appearance are noticed more on T2-weighted MRI {1409151; 11756727; 24574377}. The lesions appear as heterogeneous masses on T1- and T2-weighted images {11079622}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T15:24:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 710,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 473,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106707,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 214,
        "headingId": 473,
        "headingText": "<p>Chondromesenchymal hamartoma of the chest wall is extremely rare, with approximately 100&nbsp;cases reported in the literature {18376284}; it is usually congenital and almost all cases are diagnosed in infants {8166533; 11756727; 11528603; 3763502; 3969297; 8291008; 8861490; 1409151; 16703172}. Rare cases in older children or adults have been reported {8782339; 30374636; 32398154}. The M:F&nbsp;ratio is 2:1</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-05-10T16:15:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 711,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 474,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106708,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 214,
        "headingId": 474,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T15:24:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 712,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 475,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106709,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 214,
        "headingId": 475,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T15:24:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 719,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 482,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106710,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 214,
        "headingId": 482,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>A well-circumscribed multinodular to lobulated mass, usually 50&ndash;100&nbsp;mm. The cut surface shows blood-filled multicystic spaces, along with solid areas containing cartilage and bone {8291008; 18181344; 16703172}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T15:24:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 713,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 476,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106711,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 214,
        "headingId": 476,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumour is composed of nodules of hyaline cartilage, often with enchondral ossification, surrounding blood-filled spaces. The walls of the cystic spaces contain reactive bone, spindle cells, and osteoclastic giant cells, reminiscent of an aneurysmal bone cyst. The spindle cells lack cytological atypia and nuclear hyperchromasia {3763502; 1409151; 8291008; 11079622; 16703172; 18181344}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T15:24:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 714,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 477,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106712,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 214,
        "headingId": 477,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T15:24:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 715,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 478,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106713,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 214,
        "headingId": 478,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T15:24:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 718,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 481,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106714,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 214,
        "headingId": 481,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a well-defined solid-cystic lesion arising from the rib, composed of hyaline cartilage, blood-filled cystic spaces, woven bone, benign spindle cells, and scattered osteoclastic giant cells.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> presentation during infancy or early childhood.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T15:24:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 716,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 479,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106715,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 214,
        "headingId": 479,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T15:24:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 717,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 480,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 106716,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 214,
        "headingId": 480,
        "headingText": "<p>Chondromesenchymal hamartoma of the chest wall is a benign tumour. Rare deaths due to respiratory insufficiency have been reported {18181344; 3763502; 1409151; 8166533; 16703172}. The treatment is surgical resection. Scoliosis and deformities may be complications. Spontaneous regression may occur {11517112}; therefore, asymptomatic patients can be treated conservatively {21129530}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-04-04T10:37:24"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]